---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — MCCA Ventures LLC">
  <article class="policy">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: July 23, 2026</p>

    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy describes how MCCA Ventures LLC ("MCCA Ventures,"
      "we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, and shares information in
      connection with the mobile applications we publish (collectively, the
      "Apps") and this website. It applies across our portfolio of Apps;
      where a specific App's in-app disclosures differ from or add to this
      Policy, those disclosures control for that App.
    </p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>Depending on the specific App, we may collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Device and usage information</strong>: device type,
        operating system version, app version, crash reports, and general
        usage analytics (e.g., which features are used and how often),
        collected to help us maintain and improve our Apps.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Content you provide</strong>: information you voluntarily
        enter within an App, such as saved preferences, in-app records, or
        data you choose to track (for example, financial entries or account
        details in a personal finance app).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Approximate location</strong>: some Apps may use IP-based or
        device-provided location data to support relevant features; we do
        not collect precise location unless a specific App's in-app
        disclosures state otherwise.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not require you to create an account or provide personally
      identifiable information to use most of our Apps unless a specific
      App's in-app disclosures state otherwise — for example, an App that
      manages financial accounts may require identifying or financial
      information to function.
    </p>

    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Operate, maintain, and improve our Apps</li>
      <li>Personalize your experience within an App</li>
      <li>Diagnose technical issues and fix bugs</li>
      <li>Understand aggregate usage patterns</li>
      <li>Detect, prevent, and address fraud, abuse, or security issues</li>
      <li>Respond to you if you contact us for support</li>
      <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information. We may share information with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Service providers</strong> who help us operate our Apps
        (e.g., crash reporting, analytics, cloud hosting, or — for Apps with
        financial features — payment or account-linking providers), under
        obligations to protect your information.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal authorities</strong>, if required by law or to protect
        the rights, property, or safety of MCCA Ventures, our users, or
        others.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Business transfers</strong>: if MCCA Ventures is involved in
        a merger, acquisition, financing, or sale of assets — including the
        sale or transfer of an individual App — information may be
        transferred as part of that transaction.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data Storage and Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use reputable third-party cloud infrastructure providers to store
      and process information collected through our Apps. We take
      reasonable measures to protect that information, but no method of
      transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee
      absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      We retain information for as long as necessary to provide the Apps'
      features, comply with our legal obligations, resolve disputes, and
      enforce our agreements. Where information is used only in aggregated
      or anonymized form (for example, aggregate usage analytics), we may
      retain it for longer since it no longer identifies you.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Rights and Choices</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live and which App you use, you may have
      rights under applicable data protection laws, including the right to
      access, correct, or delete personal information we hold about you,
      and the right to withdraw consent where our processing relies on it.
      To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
      <a href="mailto:mccaventures@gmail.com">mccaventures@gmail.com</a>;
      we will respond consistent with applicable law. Because many Apps do
      not require an account or collect directly identifying information,
      we may not be able to associate data with you for these purposes
      unless you have provided identifying information within a specific
      App.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
    <p>
      This website may use cookies or similar technologies to support basic
      site functionality and analytics. You can control cookies through
      your browser settings, though disabling them may affect how this
      website functions. Our Apps may use comparable mobile technologies,
      such as device identifiers, for analytics and crash reporting; where
      an App offers in-app tracking controls, those controls are presented
      within the App itself.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      We work with third-party service providers to operate our Apps and
      this website, such as cloud hosting, analytics, and crash reporting
      providers. These providers process information on our behalf and are
      contractually obligated to protect it. We do not control third-party
      providers' own privacy practices, and we encourage you to review
      their privacy policies as well.
    </p>

    <h2>Additional Notices for Specific Jurisdictions</h2>
    <h3>European Economic Area and United Kingdom</h3>
    <p>
      If you are located in the EEA or UK, we process personal information
      on the legal bases described in this Policy — such as our legitimate
      interests in operating and improving the Apps, your consent where
      required, or as necessary to provide an App's features to you. You
      may have additional rights under the General Data Protection
      Regulation (GDPR), including the right to lodge a complaint with your
      local data protection authority.
    </p>
    <h3>California</h3>
    <p>
      If you are a California resident, you have rights under the
      California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), including the right to
      request disclosure of, and deletion of, personal information we have
      collected about you, and the right not to be discriminated against
      for exercising these rights. We do not sell personal information as
      defined under California law.
    </p>
    <h3>Other Regions</h3>
    <p>
      If you access our Apps or this website from outside the United
      States, your information may be transferred to, stored, and
      processed in the United States or other countries where our service
      providers operate. By using our Apps, you consent to this transfer.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our Apps are not directed at children under 13, and we do not
      knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you
      believe a child has provided us with personal information, please
      contact us so we can remove it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be
      posted on this page with an updated "Last updated" date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or any of our Apps,
      contact us at
      <a href="mailto:mccaventures@gmail.com">mccaventures@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="disclaimer">
      This is a general privacy policy template intended to cover a portfolio of mobile applications, including general references to frameworks such as the GDPR and CCPA. It should be reviewed by legal counsel before being relied upon for compliance purposes, and updated to reflect the specific data practices, third-party services, and legal obligations of each App as they are released.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .disclaimer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
